  "description": "The course is organized around three determinants of behavior in organizations: 1) individuals, 2) groups, and 3) organizational structure. Particular emphasis will be placed on individual difference, attitude, motivation, job satisfaction, communication, leadership, stress, change, and organizational culture. Vigorous class discussions, cases, activities, along with group projects and self quizzes will provide the basis for the learning environment in the classroom.",
  "learning_outcomes": [
    {
      "No.": "1",
      "CLO Name": "CLO1",
      "CLO Details": "Analyze the behavior of individuals and groups in organizations in terms of the key factors that influence organizational behavior"
    },
    {
      "No.": "2",
      "CLO Name": "CLO2",
      "CLO Details": "Assess the potential effects of organizational-level factors (such as structure, culture and change) on organizational behavior"
    },
    {
      "No.": "3",
      "CLO Name": "CLO3",
      "CLO Details": "Analyze organizational behavioral issues in the context of organizational behavior theories, models and concepts"
    },
    {
      "No.": "4",
      "CLO Name": "CLO4",
      "CLO Details": "Able to appropriately apply a motivational theory to a realistic motivational problem in an organizational context; able to provide management recommendations consistent with theory"
    },
    {
      "No.": "5",
      "CLO Name": "CLO5",
      "CLO Details": "Able to demonstrate an understanding of the five conflict management styles by explaining the appropriateness (advantages, disadvantages) of a particular style to a specific context"
    },
    {
      "No.": "6",
      "CLO Name": "CLO6",
      "CLO Details": "Understand what is meant by organizational culture, and able to conduct an organizational cultural assessment."
    }
  ],
